# Render and assets

Load from `assets/usable/` via `assets.FS` (`lot.json`, `tileset.png`, `sprites.png`, `sprites.json`). Older drafts (`assets/atlas.json`, `assets/lot_40x80.csv`) stay unloaded.

**Usable sheets are slot-locked.** Masters live in `assets/src/` and are not embedded. `go run ./cmd/stamp-asset` is the only writer of usable pixels (except `cmd/genfx` restamping `boom_*` / `spark_*` in place). `assets/LEDGER.md` is the slot list. Never repack; never move an existing frame rect or tile ID 0–18.

**Tiles draw the ground. Objects own AABBs.** Do not bake buildings into the tile grid and also spawn `lot.Building` from literals (double-draw). Do not use the tile layer as collision. Concrete decals are paint; solidity is `threats.Blocker`.

`lot.go` literals remain source of truth until a loader parses `lot.json` objects into `lot.New`. The Tiled object layer is a mirror — keep them in lockstep. Tiled GIDs are `localID+1`; `lot.json` uses raw IDs (0 = empty).

## Sprites

16 facings are draw-only. Frame names: `dozer_up_00`..`15` / `dozer_down_00`..`15` via `FacingIndex(heading)`.

```go
// ✅ atlas facing is already rotated
op.GeoM.Translate(sx-f.AnchorX, sy-f.AnchorY)
op.Filter = ebiten.FilterNearest
op.ColorScale.Scale(...) // plate + heat tint
```

If you blit a facing frame, do not also `GeoM.Rotate`. Plate/heat: one 16-facing set + `ColorScale` toward primer / rust / frame / `#C04040`. Preview frames in the atlas are for artists, not extra draw paths.

HUD: elapsed clock, running `$`, `×mult` if targets > 0, rim pips (sheriff amber, yard rust, plant cyan), `BLADE UP` / `BLADE DOWN`. No numeric heat or HP except the `F2` debug overlay (off by default).

Palette colors live in `internal/render/palette.go`. Draw order is impl guide §15 / `DrawWorld`.
